# Retail data (port/docs/retail-jp-plan.md, "Gore"): the Japanese discs (G4BJ08) play with the gore of the US
# release, always, without a setting (decision of the project owner, 06.11.2026; a user builds a Chinese
# translation on the Japanese discs and asked for the Ganado headshot as on the US disc). The game runs with
# country 0 for the Japanese discs (runtime/game_language.cpp: their texts, fonts, memory card names and DVD
# messages), and this build cuts the gore for country 0: a shot Ganado of the village keeps its head
# (em10LostHeadCk: only where the parasites show), the chainsaw and the head-loss deaths of Leon (em10, em25,
# em2c, em2d, em31, em32, emwep, obj16) only scream and bleed, with other camera angles, and the corpses of
# r100, r101 (also the binoculars' view of it) and r103 are left out. Every read of pSys->eff_country in these
# files is such a gore check; each now asks re4_gore_country() (runtime/game_language.cpp): the country, but the
# US release's 1 with the Japanese discs. Their data hold everything the US way needs: the models, effects and
# room entries are those of the European discs, which play it so (checked entry by entry, 06.11.2026). The Korean
# translation of the Japanese discs is a Japanese disc here too; its own code does the same (its main.dol and
# em10..em17 load 1 for every country read), patch 0147's Korean-only switch in emwep/obj16 goes into this one.
# Left as they are: r31c's tower explosion end (not gore), the texts by country and language. Debug, US and EU
# discs: unchanged. A port patch for retail data.
